    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 146\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5170, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the civil practice law and rules, in relation to\n      permitting a plaintiff to recover against a third party  defendant\n      in certain cases\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill amends the Civil Procedure Law and Rules to allow an injured\nplaintiff to directly recover from a third-party defendant on a judgment\nfor  contribution  or  indemnification  when  the defendant/third- party\nplaintiff fails to  satisfy  the  underlying  judgment  upon  which  the\ncontribution  or indemnification is based. In particular, the bill would\noverturn Court of Appeals precedent and  longstanding  State  policy  by\nrequiring  workers'  compensation  insurance  to pay for the unsatisfied\namount of any judgment obtained  by  an  injured  worker  in  applicable\ncases.\n \n  I  support  protecting  workers  and compensating those injured on the\njob, especially individuals  suffering  from  grave  injuries,  but  the\nproposed legislation is not an effective or practical means to that end.\nNumerous  stakeholders,  including  the State Insurance Fund and Workers\nCompensation Board, raised concerns with this approach, with many  stat-\ning that this change will significantly increase insurance premiums. The\nNew  York  Compensation Insurance Rating Board determined that this bill\ncould result in an increase  of  $320  million  in  additional  workers'\ncompensation  insured  loss  costs,  which  would be concentrated in the\nconstruction  industry,  resulting  in  a  nearly  twenty-five   percent\nincrease  in insurance premiums in that industry. These increased premi-\nums would fall almost exclusively on the construction industry at a time\nwhen housing and infrastructure costs are rising significantly, and cost\nof living is at the top of New Yorkers' minds.\n \n  This bill was vetoed in 2019 based on the same concerns and  the  bill\nbefore  me  has  not  been amended. Based on the foregoing reasons, I am\nconstrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
